      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <h3>Is a highbanker enough to mine gold commercially?</h3>
      <p>A highbanker is hand-fed, so the gravel it processes in a day is set by how fast a person can shovel, not by how rich the ground is. That makes it an excellent sampling and prospecting tool and a poor production machine. Once you are paying anyone to shovel, throughput is what you are actually buying, and that is what a wash plant sells.</p>

      <h3>Can I run a gold wash plant without a creek or river?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Our plants run on a recirculating settling pond rather than a live waterway. Around 500 GPM flows through a 50-ton plant, but with recirculation the actual consumption is only about 50 to 75 GPM, which is what you are topping up for evaporation and moisture leaving with the tailings.</p>

      <h3>How long does it take to get a gold wash plant running?</h3>
      <p>Most plants are built in one to three weeks depending on configuration, and custom modifications may add time. On site, setup runs about 30 minutes on our smaller plants and around an hour on the largest. You level the plant, connect water, and start feeding.</p>
